WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
[Music]

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.846
Hi, everyone, I'm Molly Wright,
a junior from Memphis, Tennessee,

3
00:00:07.846 --> 00:00:09.900
and I'm this year's
Director of Philanthropy.

4
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.100
Tri Delta's national philanthropy is
St. Jude Children's Research Hospital.

5
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.003
When a patient goes to St. Jude,
their family never

6
00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:19.300
receives a bill for their
child's lifesaving care.

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.814
Tri Delta places a housing
facility on St. Jude's campus where

8
00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:25.700
families and patients can stay
during their time at St. Jude.

9
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.721
I'm incredibly proud to be
a part of a chapter that

10
00:00:28.721 --> 00:00:31.300
focuses its ideals on such
an important organization.

11
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.966
I'm Ann Morgan Sanders. I'm from
Tupelo, Mississippi, and when I was

12
00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:39.500
just a year old, I was diagnosed
with acute lymphoblastic leukemia.

13
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.934
Going through recruitment,
Tri Delta's philanthropy really resonated

14
00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:45.700
with me because of my own
personal experience with St. Jude.

15
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.317
As recruitment week went on,
I kept thinking

16
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:50.401
back to Tri Delta's
philanthropy and thinking

17
00:00:50.401 --> 00:00:52.624
about how if I went Tri Delt,
I would be getting

18
00:00:52.624 --> 00:00:54.800
to give back to the place
that gave me so much.

19
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.099
Even though I was diagnosed at such
a young age, St. Jude still means so much

20
00:00:59.099 --> 00:01:02.800
to me because without their lifesaving
treatment, I wouldn't be here today.

21
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.000
Hey, everyone, my name is Kylie Branian.

22
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.400
I'm from Nashville, Tennessee.

23
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.724
When I was 16 years old, I was diagnosed

24
00:01:09.724 --> 00:01:12.300
with a high-risk type
of cancer called neuroblastoma.

25
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.203
After my diagnosis,
my family and I had to look

26
00:01:15.203 --> 00:01:17.300
at numerous places to receive treatment.

27
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.100
We decided that St. Jude was
the perfect place for me.

28
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.089
When I got to St. Jude,
the first place that my family

29
00:01:23.089 --> 00:01:26.300
and I stayed was the Tri Delta
Place on St. Jude's campus.

30
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.365
For a little under two years,
I went through numerous

31
00:01:30.365 --> 00:01:34.000
rounds of chemotherapy, radiation,
transplants and surgery.

32
00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.746
The nurses and staff at St. Jude helped
me through some of my hardest days,

33
00:01:37.746 --> 00:01:39.900
even though I wasn't able
to be home very often.

34
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.121
Little did I know, three years
later, I'd be sitting here

35
00:01:43.121 --> 00:01:45.900
today next to someone who shares
such a similar story to me.

36
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.250
Throughout the year,
we host several different

37
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.100
fundraising events to raise
money for St. Jude.

38
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.515
Not only are we raising
money and saving lives,

39
00:01:52.515 --> 00:01:54.400
but we're also bonding with our sisters.

40
00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.647
One of our biggest
fundraising events is DHOP,

41
00:01:57.647 --> 00:01:59.800
which we hold each year
at the Tri Delta house.

42
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.576
DHOP is our pancake breakfast
where all our members sell

43
00:02:03.576 --> 00:02:06.500
tickets to the students on
campus and the Oxford community.

44
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.630
This event is so fun because
all members of the community

45
00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.100
get to come out to the house
to support our philanthropy.

46
00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.636
In the spring, we host our annual
letter-writing campaign where all

47
00:02:15.636 --> 00:02:18.700
our members ask their friends
and families for donations to St. Jude.

48
00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.147
One good thing about being so
close to Memphis is that so many

49
00:02:22.147 --> 00:02:25.300
of us got to participate
in the St. Jude Half Marathon this year.

50
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.841
I, along with so many
others, had the honor

51
00:02:27.841 --> 00:02:30.400
of running through St. Jude
campus in December.

52
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.487
One unique event that we
get to host at the Chi

53
00:02:32.487 --> 00:02:34.600
chapter is our Shirley Crawford
Tennis Tournament.

54
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.447
It's so amazing to see so many people
come out to support our beloved alum,

55
00:02:38.447 --> 00:02:41.300
Shirley Crawford, and to support
our philanthropy, St. Jude.

56
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.394
When Tri Delta first made its
partnership with St. Jude,

57
00:02:44.394 --> 00:02:46.960
we committed to raising
$60 million in 10 years.

58
00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.794
And I'm so excited to tell
you all that this past year,

59
00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:51.700
we reached that goal two years early.

60
00:02:52.000 --> 00:03:23.200
[Music]
